message: "Please cite the specific version of this work that you use."
type: article
title: "Covering versus hitting in diversity embeddings: an affine obstruction and matching bounds"
authors:
  - family-names: Kline
    given-names: Jeff
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/jeff-kline/covering-hitting-diversities"
license: GPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - diversities
  - hypergraph sparsest cut
  - affine geometry
  - coverage functions
abstract: >-
  A compact affine hypergraph realizes square-root diversity distortion with
  polynomial encoding size and a specified connector-LP gap. The existential
  lower bound and finite constant follow from earlier set-function work;
  priority of the compact realization remains unresolved. Matching exponents
  hold for unit-cost pairwise-intersecting supplies, not arbitrary hypergraphs.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22731697"
date-released: "2026-09-13"
